SECTION 1: KUBERNETES OVERVIEW & ARCHITECTURE
Kubernetes
What is Kubernetes?

Kubernetes (K8s) is an open-source container orchestration platform used to deploy, manage, scale, monitor, and maintain containerized applications.

It automates:

Deployment
Scaling
Self-healing
Service discovery
Load balancing
Rolling updates
Why Kubernetes?

Without Kubernetes:

Application Crash
      ↓
Manual Restart

With Kubernetes:

Application Crash
      ↓
Pod Fails
      ↓
Kubernetes Detects Failure
      ↓
New Pod Created Automatically
Ecommerce Project Example

Our project contains:

Angular Frontend
Node.js Backend
MySQL Database

Kubernetes manages all these components.

