SECTION 3: SERVICES → DNS → SERVICE DISCOVERY → CLUSTERIP → NODEPORT → INGRESS
Why Services?

Pods are temporary.

Example:

backend-pod-1
IP = 10.244.0.10

Pod crashes:

backend-pod-2
IP = 10.244.0.25

Problem:

Frontend still trying to call:

10.244.0.10

Application breaks.

Solution

Use a Service.

Service provides:

Permanent Name
Permanent IP
Load Balancing
Service Discovery
Service Architecture
Frontend Pod
      |
      |
      v
ecommerce-backend-service
      |
      |
      +----------------+
      |                |
      v                v
Backend Pod-1    Backend Pod-2
What is a Service?

A Service is a stable network endpoint that exposes one or more Pods.

Ecommerce Example

Instead of calling:

10.244.0.10
10.244.0.11

Frontend calls:

ecommerce-backend-service

Kubernetes routes traffic automatically.

How Service Finds Pods

Using Labels.

Backend Pods:

labels:
  app: ecommerce-backend

Service:

selector:
  app: ecommerce-backend
Visual Flow
Service Selector
      |
      |
app=ecommerce-backend
      |
      |
      +------------+
      |            |
      v            v
Backend Pod   Backend Pod
